      economy: "Lithuania is a high-income member of the EU and eurozone and the largest economy among the Baltic states, with recovery driven by private consumption and EU fund-backed investment. Its export base includes refined petroleum, furniture, plastic products, wheat, and cars, while industries range from shipbuilding and petroleum refining to lasers, biotechnology, and video game development. Structural challenges include pension reform, an aging workforce, and high costs from imported energy.",
      people_and_culture: "The population is predominantly Lithuanian (84.6%), with Polish, Russian, and Belarusian minorities. Roman Catholicism is the dominant religion at 74.2%, alongside smaller communities of Russian Orthodox, Old Believer, Evangelical Lutheran, and Evangelical Reformist adherents, plus small Sunni Muslim, Jewish, Greek Catholic, and Karaite populations.",
