      economy: "Moldova is an upper middle-income economy that saw sustained growth reversed by COVID-19. It relies significantly on remittances from citizens working abroad, and depends on Russian energy along with broader regional economic ties. As an agricultural exporter, its outbound trade includes insulated wire, garments, refined petroleum, seed oils, and wheat, alongside industries such as sugar processing, vegetable oil and food processing, agricultural machinery, foundry equipment, refrigerators and freezers, washing machines, hosiery, shoes, and textiles. The workforce is declining, driven by emigration and low fertility.",
