      economy: "Mauritius is an upper middle-income island economy with a diversified portfolio, including investment in maritime security and expansion into information and financial services. Tourism has long been a strong sector but was decimated by COVID-19. Industries include food processing, largely sugar milling, along with textiles, clothing, mining, chemicals, metal products, transport equipment, and nonelectrical machinery, while exports include fish, garments, raw sugar, fertilizers, and diamonds. The economy is described as environmentally fragile.",
      people_and_culture: "The population is majority Creole-speaking (86.5%), with Bhojpuri and French also spoken; English, though an official language of the National Assembly, is spoken by less than 1% of people. Religiously, the country is nearly half Hindu (48.5%), with Roman Catholic (26.3%), Muslim (17.3%), and other Christian (6.4%) communities as well. Ethnically, Indo-Mauritians make up about two thirds of the population, alongside Creole, Sino-Mauritian, and Franco-Mauritian communities.",
