      climate: "The climate ranges from tropical to subtropical. Central and southern provinces are vulnerable to severe droughts as well as devastating cyclones and floods.",
      economy: "Mozambique is a low-income economy in which subsistence farming still dominates the labor force, though growth has returned on the strength of agriculture and extractive industries. Exports are led by coal, natural gas, aluminum, gold, and precious stones, while industry produces aluminum, petroleum products, chemicals such as fertilizer, soap, and paints, textiles, cement, glass, asbestos, tobacco, food, and beverages. The country is working through a foreign debt restructuring under the IMF's Highly Indebted Poor Countries initiative.",
      people_and_culture: "Makhuwa is the largest first language at 26.1%, followed by Portuguese, the official language, at 16.6%, with Tsonga, Nyanja, Sena, Lomwe, Chuwabo, Ndau, and Tswa also spoken. Religious life is similarly varied: Catholics make up 27.3% of the population, Muslims 19.1%, Pentecostals 16.7%, and followers of Saio/Zione churches 16.3%, alongside a substantial share, 13.5%, with no religion. Ethnically the population is 99% African, drawn from groups including the Makhuwa, Tsonga, Lomwe, and Sena, with small Mestizo and other minorities.",
