      climate: "Conditions vary sharply by region, from hot, dry desert across most of the country to temperate in the northwest and arctic in the north. Earthquakes occur frequently and can be severe, particularly in the north and west, while heavy rains in July and August often bring flooding along the Indus River.",
      economy: "Pakistan is a lower middle-income South Asian economy carrying extremely high debt, with endemic corruption and regional disputes with India and Afghanistan discouraging investment. Falling inflation, IMF relief programs, and strong agricultural output are slowly contributing to recovery. Key industries include textiles and apparel, food processing, pharmaceuticals, surgical instruments, construction materials, paper products, fertilizer and shrimp, with garments, fabric, refined petroleum, rice and cotton fabric as leading exports.",
      people_and_culture: "The population is overwhelmingly Muslim at 96.4%, with Hindu (1.6%) and Christian (1.4%) minorities, alongside smaller communities including scheduled castes, Qadiani/Ahmadi, and Sikh groups. Ethnically, Punjabis form the largest group at 44.7%, followed by Pashtuns (Pathans) at 15.4%, Sindhis at 14.1%, Saraikis at 8.4%, Muhajirs at 7.6%, and Baloch at 3.6%.",
      _sources: {"prose":"CIA World Factbook (public domain)","structured":"Wikidata (CC0)"},
