      climate: "The climate is mostly desert, hot and humid along the west coast, temperate in the western mountains where seasonal monsoons have an effect, and extraordinarily hot, dry, and harsh in the eastern desert. Sandstorms and dust storms occur in summer. There is limited volcanic activity, including Jebel at Tair, an island volcano in the Red Sea that became active in 2007, along with other historically active volcanoes such as Harra of Arhab and Harras of Dhamar, though many have not erupted in over a century.",
